    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **254 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` test asserting the new format.\n\n## Summary\n\nChanged the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a **per-city** sequence.\n\n**`AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the sole place customerCode is built:\n- CITY3 = upper-cased first three letters of the owner's `city`\n- LAST3 = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`\n- NNNN = 4-digit zero-padded sequence = one more than the count of owners already in that same city (computed by filtering `findAll()` by city, since the owner isn't saved yet). Previously this was a global count.\n\n**Derived values rebuild automatically:** the `membershipNumber` in `OwnerMapper` is built as `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, so it now reads e.g. `LON-SMI-0007-M26` with no code change needed \u2014 it reflects the new customerCode format directly.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` descriptions and examples to document the new `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` format.\n\nNo repository change was required: the per-city count reuses the existing `findAll()` and filters on `owner.getCity()`.",
